 "standard_text": "Investigate and describe the properties of the sides, angles and diagonals of quadrilaterals; solve geometric problems involving unknown sides and angles in quadrilaterals using known properties.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 9 quadrilaterals worksheets: angles, properties and diagonals of quadrilaterals and angle sums of polygons. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "Polygon: (n − 2) × 180°.",
 "key_sub": "Exterior angles add to 360°.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>The angles of a quadrilateral add up to 360°.</li><li>Parallelogram: opposite sides parallel and equal, diagonals bisect each other. Rhombus: diagonals perpendicular. Rectangle: diagonals equal.</li><li>Angle sum of an n-sided polygon: (n − 2) × 180°.</li><li>Exterior angles of any polygon add up to 360°.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>A regular polygon with exterior angle 30°</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>360 ÷ 30</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 12 sides</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>180° for a quadrilateral</td><td>It is 360°.</td></tr><tr><td>All diagonals equal</td><td>Only in rectangles and squares.</td></tr><tr><td>n × 180°</td><td>Use (n − 2) × 180°.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
